  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(120.68pt, 372.98pt, " Schematic of the optical setup for the FTIR spectrum. ‘M1’ and ‘M2’ represent reflective ")
  #line-at(72pt, 388.58pt, "mirrors. ‘Pol’ and ‘BS’ refer to polarizer and beam-splitter, respectively. CPA stands for current pre-")
  #line-at(72pt, 404.18pt, "amplifier. The red lines represent infrared light beams, and the black lines represent the electric wires.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(92.9pt, 433.96pt, "The photodetector performance was characterized by the optical setup illustrated in Figure ")
  #line-at(72pt, 465.16pt, "S2. Infrared light from a Fourier-transform infrared (FTIR) spectrometer (Bruker Vertex 70) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 496.36pt, "was passed through a polarizer, a beam splitter, and a chopper before being focused onto the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 527.56pt, "sample by a Cassegrain objective lens (Thorlabs LMM40X-UVV). The generated photocurrent ")
  #line-at(72pt, 558.76pt, "was collected by electrical probes, then amplified sequentially by a current pre-amplifier (CPA) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 589.96pt, "and a lock-in amplifier. The resulting signal was returned to the FTIR for processing. The use ")
  #line-at(72pt, 621.16pt, "of a chopper, synchronized with the CPA and lock-in amplifier, significantly enhanced the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 652.36pt, "signal-to-noise ratio. The FTIR spectrum was obtained by recording the signal while varying ")
  #line-at(72pt, 683.56pt, "the optical path length difference in the interferometer, followed by a Fourier transformation ")
  #line-at(72pt, 714.78pt, "to the recorded interferogram. Finally, the FTIR spectrum was normalized by the power ")
  #line-at(72pt, 745.98pt, "spectrum of the light source of FTIR. ")
]

