  #line-at(92.9pt, 347.54pt, "The absolute responsivity of the photodetector was measured using the setup depicted in ")
  #line-at(72pt, 378.74pt, "Figure S3. The FTIR was replaced with a 1.55 μm infrared laser. The laser beam, with an optical ")
  #line-at(72pt, 409.94pt, "power of 1.26 mW, was focused onto the GeSn membrane with a spot size of 7 μm in diameter. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 441.16pt, "The photocurrent and dark current were measured using a source measure unit (SMU, Keithley ")
  #line-at(72pt, 472.36pt, "2470). To ensure the laser was optimally focused on the membrane, the sample stage was ")
  #line-at(72pt, 503.56pt, "carefully adjusted until the photoresponse was maximized. Subsequently, current–voltage (I–")
  #line-at(72pt, 534.76pt, "V) characteristics were recorded with or without laser illumination to measure photo and dark ")
  #line-at(72pt, 565.96pt, "currents. The photocurrent was calculated by subtracting the dark current from the total current ")
  #line-at(72pt, 597.16pt, "measured under laser illumination. ")
